    {
      "id": "claim_4441eeb311644301b59e31689910ef52",
      "statement": "deep16_core3.sv takes a level IRQ at an instruction boundary (irq && PSW.I && !PSW.S && !delay_active), replaces the decoded word with a synthetic SWI selecting vector 1, parks the interrupted PSW, enters with PSW=0x0020 (S=1, I=0), zeroes the shadow segment registers and loads the shadow PC from the vector; the parked instruction is the one about to execute, so RETI re-runs it.",
